-- The ESP32-C3's memory for a RAM-only image, which the boot ROM loads
-- from flash offset 0 and enters with no second stage (D707).  Written by
-- hand; see devices/README.md for the sources it was checked against.
--
-- SRAM1's 384 KiB are one memory at two addresses: the instruction bus's
-- 0x4038_0000 and the data bus's 0x3FC8_0000, 0x70_0000 apart (TRM v1.4,
-- 3.3.2, Table 3.3-1, pp. 93 and 94).  Code takes the first 128 KiB
-- through the instruction bus and data the 160 KiB from 0x3FCA_0000,
-- which is the memory after the code's, so neither region reaches the
-- other's bytes.  Both end below 0x3FCC_AE00, where the ROM's download
-- buffers, its stack and its own data begin (ESP-IDF v6.1's
-- bootloader.memory.ld.in): the ROM loads the image without writing a
-- byte of it.  The 16 KiB below 0x4038_0000 are the instruction cache's
-- and are not described.
--
-- The image header names the chip, ESP-IDF v6.1's esp_app_format.h's
-- esp_chip_id_t, 5, and the revisions it runs on, ESP-IDF v6.1's
-- defaults in components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32c3/Kconfig.hw_support:
-- from v0.3 (ECO3), 3, to v1.99, 199; the ROM reads it at flash offset 0.
--
-- The image runs from SRAM: no flash is mapped and no cache is enabled.

linker.region("IRAM", 0x4038_0000, 128 * 1024, "rx")
linker.region("DRAM", 0x3FCA_0000, 160 * 1024, "rw")
compiler.boot("esp-app-image")
compiler.esp_image(5, 3, 199, 0x0)
linker.place("vectors", "IRAM")
linker.place("text", "IRAM")
linker.place("rodata", "IRAM")
linker.place("data", "DRAM")
linker.place("bss", "DRAM")
linker.place("stack", "DRAM", 16 * 1024)
